SED
----
SED=Stream Editor
- Retrieve, delete and edit data.

retrieve=awk
delete,edit=sed
-Realtime mostly use this 2 command not cut command

Print all rows
--------------
[ec2-user@ip-172-31-1-83 ~]$ sed 'p' data.txt
java|2000|language
java|2000|language
mysql|5000|database
mysql|5000|database
oracle|4000|database
oracle|4000|database
python|3000|langauge
python|3000|langauge
django|3000|language
django|3000|language

-It show 2 times for one time use -n
-------------------------------------
[ec2-user@ip-172-31-1-83 ~]$ sed -n 'p' data.txt
java|2000|language
mysql|5000|database
oracle|4000|database
python|3000|langauge
django|3000|language

Print only 2nd line
-------------------
In awk= 
[ec2-user@ip-172-31-1-83 ~]$ awk 'NR==2 {print}' data.txt
mysql|5000|database
In sed = 
[ec2-user@ip-172-31-1-83 ~]$ sed -n '2p' data.txt
mysql|5000|database

Print all lines insted of line 2
--------------------------------
In awk
[ec2-user@ip-172-31-1-83 ~]$ awk 'NR!=2 {print}' data.txt
java|2000|language
oracle|4000|database
python|3000|langauge
django|3000|language

In sed
[ec2-user@ip-172-31-1-83 ~]$ sed -n '2!p' data.txt
java|2000|language
oracle|4000|database
python|3000|langauge
django|3000|language

-For retriving allways use awk .
-For delete , edit use sed .

Delete 
------
Q.Delete 1st line 

[ec2-user@ip-172-31-1-83 ~]$ sed '1d' data3.txt
mysql|5000|database
oracle|4000|database
python|3000|langauge
django|3000|language

Delete 1st line and copy to new file then update to original file
-----------------------------------------------------------------
[ec2-user@ip-172-31-1-83 ~]$ sed '1d' data.txt > data7.txt
[ec2-user@ip-172-31-1-83 ~]$ cat data7.txt
mysql|5000|database
oracle|4000|database
python|3000|langauge
django|3000|language
[ec2-user@ip-172-31-1-83 ~]$ cp data7.txt data.txt
[ec2-user@ip-172-31-1-83 ~]$ cat data.txt
mysql|5000|database
oracle|4000|database
python|3000|langauge
django|3000|language

Q.Delete data from the file directly
-------------------------------------
[ec2-user@ip-172-31-1-83 ~]$ cat data.txt
java|2000|language
mysql|5000|database
oracle|4000|database
python|3000|langauge
django|3000|language

Copy th result to new file
--------------------------
Approach-1
-----------
[ec2-user@ip-172-31-1-83 ~]$ sed '1d' data.txt > data2.txt
[ec2-user@ip-172-31-1-83 ~]$ cat data.txt
java|2000|language
mysql|5000|database
oracle|4000|database
python|3000|langauge
django|3000|language
[ec2-user@ip-172-31-1-83 ~]$ cat data2.txt
mysql|5000|database
oracle|4000|database
python|3000|langauge
django|3000|language

-Copy the result into original(data.txt) file
[ec2-user@ip-172-31-1-83 ~]$ cp data2.txt data.txt
[ec2-user@ip-172-31-1-83 ~]$ cat data.txt
mysql|5000|database
oracle|4000|database
python|3000|langauge
django|3000|language

Approach-2 (-i)
----------
[ec2-user@ip-172-31-1-83 ~]$ cat data.txt
mysql|5000|database
oracle|4000|database
python|3000|langauge
django|3000|language
[ec2-user@ip-172-31-1-83 ~]$ sed '1d' data.txt
oracle|4000|database
python|3000|langauge
django|3000|language
[ec2-user@ip-172-31-1-83 ~]$ cat data.txt -It can't delete permanently
mysql|5000|database
oracle|4000|database
python|3000|langauge
django|3000|language

For permanently delete use (-i)
-------------------------------
[ec2-user@ip-172-31-1-83 ~]$ sed -i '1d' data.txt
[ec2-user@ip-172-31-1-83 ~]$ cat data.txt
oracle|4000|database
python|3000|langauge
django|3000|language

Edits the file in place and creates a backup file(sed -i.bak.txt)
-----------------------------------------------------------------
[ec2-user@ip-172-31-1-83 ~]$ sed -i.bak '1d' data.txt
[ec2-user@ip-172-31-1-83 ~]$ cat data.txt
python|3000|langauge
django|3000|language
[ec2-user@ip-172-31-1-83 ~]$ ls -l
total 16
-rw-r--r--. 1 ec2-user ec2-user  43 May 27 15:49 data.txt
-rw-r--r--. 1 ec2-user ec2-user  65 May 27 12:44 data.txt.bak
-rw-r--r--. 1 ec2-user ec2-user  86 May 27 12:37 data2.txt
-rw-r--r--. 1 ec2-user ec2-user 106 May 27 11:13 data3.txt
[ec2-user@ip-172-31-1-83 ~]$

-See data.txt.bak
[ec2-user@ip-172-31-1-83 ~]$ cat data.txt.bak
oracle|4000|database
python|3000|langauge
django|3000|language

Substitute Operation/Change the data
-------------------------------------
sed 's/mysql/mysql2/' data.txt 
s = substitute 

Example
------
[ec2-user@ip-172-31-1-83 ~]$ cat data.txt
python|3000|langauge
django|3000|language

-Change Python to py
[ec2-user@ip-172-31-1-83 ~]$ sed 's/python/py/' data.txt
py|3000|langauge
django|3000|language

-But it can't change permanently
-For permanent(-i)
------------------
[ec2-user@ip-172-31-1-83 ~]$ cat data.txt
python|3000|langauge
django|3000|language
[ec2-user@ip-172-31-1-83 ~]$

[ec2-user@ip-172-31-1-83 ~]$ sed -i 's/python/py/' data.txt
[ec2-user@ip-172-31-1-83 ~]$ cat data.txt
py|3000|langauge
django|3000|language

-If you recover to original then copy the data.txt.bak file





